The Queen biopic Bohemian Rhapsody is loaded
with moments, songs and details that many

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:09.250
fans will doubtless love, but did you catch
them all?

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:13.170
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here
and in this video, I'm revealing six crazy

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:16.080
little details, secrets and easter eggs you
might have missed in the movie.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.110
Keep watching to the end to find out which
Queen band member had a hidden cameo in the

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:21.110
film.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:25.270
And subscribe and leave a comment about the
movie for a chance to win some awesome Bohemian

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.060
Rhapsody merch.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:31.220
You can spot the inspiration behind the cover
art for Queen's second album in the opening

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:35.680
scene of the movie when Freddie walks past
an iconic portrait of Marlene Dietrich from

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.890
her 1932 Oscar-winning movie Shanghai Express.

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:42.760
The renowned photographer Mick Rock had been
hired by Queen to come up with a striking

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.310
image for their second album "Queen II".

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:49.180
After Rock discovered a picture of Dietrich
with her arms crossed and lit from above with

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:52.570
a top light, he proposed the look for the
band's album cover.

00:00:52.570 --> 00:00:57.739
They agreed and Freddie even imitated Dietrich's
arms crossed and fingers spread pose.

00:00:57.739 --> 00:01:02.020
And a shot of the band lit in a similar way
appears as the opening of their Bohemian Rhapsody

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.579
music video.

00:01:03.579 --> 00:01:08.249
After Freddie tells Paul Prenter to organize
a spectacular party at his home, the movie

00:01:08.249 --> 00:01:11.560
gives us a glimpse at some of the singer's
legendary events.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.670
And when they designed the set for the big
party scene, the filmmakers deliberately included

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:18.430
"references to Freddie's interests and Queen's
history".

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:23.639
In fact, there's a moment where Freddie passes
by two scantily-clad women riding a couple

00:01:23.639 --> 00:01:25.340
of stationary bikes.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:29.529
That's an easter egg to Queen's "Bicycle Race"
single, which was released as a double A-side

00:01:29.529 --> 00:01:31.439
with "Fat Bottomed Girls".

00:01:31.439 --> 00:01:35.669
The music video for "Bicycle Race" is famous
for being filmed with many nude models all

00:01:35.669 --> 00:01:39.340
racing around on bicycles at Wimbledon Stadium.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:43.939
Mike Myers makes a fun cameo in the movie
as fictional EMI executive Ray Foster who

00:01:43.939 --> 00:01:48.679
refuses to release "Bohemian Rhapsody" because
it's too long and radio stations won't play

00:01:48.679 --> 00:01:49.679
it.

00:01:49.679 --> 00:01:52.939
Among Foster's many complaints about the song
is a little inside joke.

00:01:52.939 --> 00:01:57.289
He tells Queen that "Bohemian Rhapsody" will
never be the kind of song that teenagers will

00:01:57.289 --> 00:02:00.869
crank up the volume in their car and start
head banging to.

00:02:00.869 --> 00:02:05.649
Which is funny because, of course, that's
exactly what Mike Myers did back in 1992 in

00:02:05.649 --> 00:02:10.259
the movie Wayne's World when he and his friends
played Bohemian Rhapsody in their car and

00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:15.330
started head-banging along to the
Fun fact: for Wayne's World, Mike Myers actually

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:20.689
had to fight the studio to get Bohemian Rhapsody
in the film as the producers originally wanted

00:02:20.689 --> 00:02:24.840
Guns 'N' Roses instead as they were very popular
when the movie was being made.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:29.200
After Wayne's World was released though, that
memorable moment brought Queen back into the

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:34.530
spotlight in the US and when Bohemian Rhapsody
was re-released, the song reached No. 2 on

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:36.969
the Billboard Hot 100.

00:02:36.969 --> 00:02:40.099
The Live Aid performance is one of the highlights
of Bohemian Rhapsody.

00:02:40.099 --> 00:02:45.439
There were, of course, many famous bands on
stage that day, and if you look very carefully

00:02:45.439 --> 00:02:49.769
in the scene at the start of the film as Freddie
is going on stage, just coming off stage is

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:54.659
a young Bono, the lead singer for U2, plus
you can spot his three U2 bandmates following

00:02:54.659 --> 00:02:55.760
behind him.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:59.980
It's a fun nod because at the time Queen and
U2's performances were considered by many

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.680
to be the best of the day.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.459
And by the way, look carefully in the crowd
shots as there's also a banner which reads

00:03:05.459 --> 00:03:06.659
"We Love U2".

00:03:06.659 --> 00:03:11.970
Although this moment in the film implies U2
played Live Aid right before Queen, in reality

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:15.030
it was Dire Straits who were on stage [just]
before Freddie and co.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:19.010
However, just before we see that scene again
at the end of the film, I think you can hear

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:23.069
Dire Straits' music playing in the background
over various shots including Freddie and his

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:25.099
bandmates waiting in their trailer.

00:03:25.099 --> 00:03:28.709
By the way, if you'd like to find out about
some bigger changes the movie made to Queen's

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:33.090
real-life story, you can watch my other video
which I'll link at the end and in the video

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:34.420
description.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:38.689
While original Queen bandmates Brian May and
Roger Taylor were involved in Bohemian Rhapsody

00:03:38.689 --> 00:03:43.299
behind the scenes as producers, they didn't
make on-screen cameo unless they were heavily

00:03:43.299 --> 00:03:45.129
disguised as Mike Myers was.

00:03:45.129 --> 00:03:49.290
However, who did appear was Queen's new lead
vocalist Adam Lambert.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:54.069
The former American Idol star, who has collaborated
with Queen for over six years, made a cameo

00:03:54.069 --> 00:03:55.370
as a trucker.

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:58.819
Lambert appears in the scene where Freddie
is on tour in the US and talking on the phone

00:03:58.819 --> 00:04:01.360
to Mary who's back home in England.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:05.370
Lambert's trucker then catches Freddie's eye
before going into the men's public restroom.

